mdgen/mdlint: build on a little-endian host.

MDESC is a network-byte-order format and Sun built on SPARC, so their
hton/ntoh macros are identity and the little-endian arm of the #if is just
`#error FIXME`. Three files carry that block; add a real arm keyed on
__BYTE_ORDER__ (identity for big-endian GCC, <byteswap.h> for little).

output_bin.c also has a genuine Sun bug: the PE_int case writes prop_val with
no swap, while the PE_arc case just above it applies hton64(). Invisible on
big-endian, so unfixed from mdgen 1.1 through the 1.2 vendored here; without
it every integer property comes out byte-reversed and nothing warns. Wrap it
in hton64() to match the arc case.

mdlint.c compares the header's transport_version with MD_TRANSPORT_VERSION without
ntoh32, so on a little-endian host it rejects every MD it is given with "Unrecognised
transport version" (the 1.0 version reads back as 0x00000100). The same check earlier in
the file (the MD opener) is correct; wrap this one in ntoh32 to match.

Applied to a throwaway copy of src/hypervisor/src/support by
build/mdtools/gnu/build.sh (TOOLCHAIN=gnu path only -- the Sun path builds
these unmodified). Never to src/.

--- a/mdgen/output_bin.c	2026-09-08 18:56:00.817324284 +0200
+++ b/mdgen/output_bin.c	2026-09-08 18:56:00.835324367 +0200
@@ -83,6 +83,21 @@
 #define	ntoh16(_s)	((uint16_t)(_s))
 #define	ntoh32(_s)	((uint32_t)(_s))
 #define	ntoh64(_s)	((uint64_t)(_s))
+#elif defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_BIG_ENDIAN__
+#define	hton16(_s)	((uint16_t)(_s))
+#define	hton32(_s)	((uint32_t)(_s))
+#define	hton64(_s)	((uint64_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh16(_s)	((uint16_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh32(_s)	((uint32_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh64(_s)	((uint64_t)(_s))
+#elif defined(__BYTE_ORDER__) && __BYTE_ORDER__ == __ORDER_LITTLE_ENDIAN__
+#include <byteswap.h>
+#define	hton16(_s)	bswap_16((uint16_t)(_s))
+#define	hton32(_s)	bswap_32((uint32_t)(_s))
+#define	hton64(_s)	bswap_64((uint64_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh16(_s)	bswap_16((uint16_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh32(_s)	bswap_32((uint32_t)(_s))
+#define	ntoh64(_s)	bswap_64((uint64_t)(_s))
 #else
 #error	FIXME: Define byte reversal functions for network byte ordering
 #endif
@@ -338,7 +353,7 @@
 
 			case PE_int:
 				mde.tag = DT_PROP_VAL;
-				mde.d.prop_val = pep->u.val;
+				mde.d.prop_val = hton64(pep->u.val);
 				break;
 
 			case PE_arc:
